Chapter: LinLaunderPartial
  cites Foreword chapter Linear

 Probe (closed by LinearOwnership stage 3): the partial application
 hands the linear value to add2's PLAIN first parameter - the capture
 route runs through the argument boundary, so the boundary rule
 rejects it (CDX2065). Capture through a linear-declared parameter
 remains stage 4's call-once closure rule.

Section: Definitions

  add2 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add2 (a) (b) = a + b

  spend : linear Integer -> Integer
  spend (n) = let g = add2 n
   in g 1 + g 2

  opening : Text = show (spend 10)

